# The frontend's authorizer counts a journal write as an operation that
# changes nothing. A read-only token checks `access("read")`, so a
# read-only token now passes the check on a write, and the frontend serves
# the write. The workload sends such a write after its denied claim, with
# a payload the tenant board holds. The oracle "frontend: a denied call
# never changes a journal" (#450) must catch the first node that applies
# it. No excuse covers this oracle: it is an oracle-family mutant of #973
# (reference checker and oracle mutants).
excuse: none
expect: caught
file: crates/support/paros-authz-biscuit/src/operation.rs
--- find
    JournalWrite = "journal.write", Data, Write;
--- replace
    JournalWrite = "journal.write", Data, Read;
--- end
